NOTICE — third-party code under tools/

These are differential-test oracles and probes, rescued from session scratch
directories where they had never been under version control. They are NOT shipped
code: nothing here is built by `cargo build` at the repository root, and no mdrdp
binary links any of it.

Several of these files contain, or are derived from, third-party source, modified
for the experiment each one serves. Those modifications are described below.


FreeRDP — https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP — Apache License 2.0
Copyright the FreeRDP contributors.

  codec-oracles/dwtdiff/ref.c
  codec-oracles/dwtdiff/probe.c
      progressive_rfx_idwt_x and progressive_rfx_idwt_y, adapted from
      libfreerdp/codec/progressive.c. The two files carry an identical copy of
      this body and differ only in their harness main().

  codec-oracles/rlgrdiff/src/main.rs  (decode_ref, RefBs, lzcnt_s)
      A Rust transcription of rfx_rlgr_decode, from libfreerdp/codec/rfx_rlgr.c.

  codec-oracles/py/srl_diff.py  (class FreeRdpSrl)
      A Python transcription of progressive_rfx_srl_read, from
      libfreerdp/codec/progressive.c.

  codec-oracles/py/dwt_diff.py  (c_block)
      A Python transcription of rfx_dwt_2d_decode_block, from
      libfreerdp/codec/rfx_dwt.c.

  codec-oracles/py/cmp.py  (ref_bgrx, ref_gen)
      The fixed-point YCbCr-to-RGB constants from
      libfreerdp/primitives/prim_colors.c.

  codec-oracles/refdec.c calls FreeRDP through its public headers and links the
      installed library. It embeds no FreeRDP source.

  codec-oracles/avc444diff/shim.c likewise calls FreeRDP through its public
      headers (freerdp/primitives.h, freerdp/codec/color.h) and links the
      installed libfreerdp3 and libwinpr3. It embeds no FreeRDP source.
      codec-oracles/avc444diff/tests/differential.rs contains one four-line
      transcription of the fixed-point YUV-to-RGB matrix from
      libfreerdp/primitives/prim_internal.h, used as a negative control.

  UNVERIFIED, and it matters: no FreeRDP source tree exists on the machine these
  were rescued on, so ref.c and probe.c could not be diffed against upstream
  progressive.c. They retain FreeRDP's own spellings (WINPR_RESTRICT, INT16, its
  full parameter lists), so they may be closer to verbatim than "adapted"
  suggests. Anyone extending them should do that diff and, if they are verbatim,
  give them FreeRDP's own file header in place of this summary.


